 ## Background
-Gabor noise was introduced by Lagae et al. in 2009 [S1, S2, S3]. It was presented in the paper "A Survey of Procedural Noise Functions" and related works [LLDD09a, LLDD09b, LLD09] [S1, S2, S3]. The method extends the framework of sparse convolution noise by introducing the Gabor kernel, which combines a Gaussian envelope with a cosine wave [S1, S3]. It is used for setup-free surface noise and analytic anisotropic filtering of noise [S1, S3].
